\ Spitfire: the clouds. Cumulus stand on a common base, each a cluster of
\ spheres in a 3 km square of the sky chosen by a hash of the square's
\ position, so the same clouds are there whenever the aircraft returns; the
\ mission sets the share of squares that hold one and the base's height.
\ The spheres within 15 km of the aircraft are gathered again only when it
\ crosses into another square. Each frame every sphere in view is drawn as
\ a filled disc, the upper spheres lighter than the lower, faded into the
\ sky with distance; the discs and the bombers are drawn together from the
\ farthest to the nearest, so a bomber in front of a cloud shows and one
\ behind it is hidden. With the eye inside a sphere the whole view is the
\ cloud's colour, and only the instruments tell which way is up. Each cloud
\ casts its shadow on the ground, its footprint moved north by the base's
\ height over the tangent of the sun's elevation, a darker polygon drawn
\ after the ground's fill.

3000 constant cloud-square
5 constant cloud-reach

variable cloud-cover
0 to cloud-cover
variable cloud-base
1500 to cloud-base
variable cloud-squares
{ } to cloud-squares
variable cloud-square-at
[ null null ] to cloud-square-at
variable cloud-centres
0 4 0-matrix to cloud-centres
variable cloud-radii
0 1 0-matrix to cloud-radii
variable cloud-shades
0 1 0-matrix to cloud-shades
variable in-cloud
false to in-cloud

\ the weather's clouds: the share of squares holding one and the height of their base; the clouds gathered before are forgotten
: use-clouds ( cover base -- )
	| cover base ^cloud-cover ^cloud-base ^cloud-squares ^cloud-square-at |
	cover to cloud-cover
	base to cloud-base
	{ } to cloud-squares
	[ null null ] to cloud-square-at ;

\ one square's cloud as spheres [ x y z radius shade ], the shade 0 at the base and near 1 at the top; none when the hash leaves the square clear
: square-cloud ( column row -- spheres )
	| column row |
	column 7.31 * row 13.17 * + 101 + to seed
	seed hash-fraction cloud-cover >= if [ ] exit then
	column 0.2 + seed 1.1 + hash-fraction 0.6 * + cloud-square * to x
	row 0.2 + seed 2.3 + hash-fraction 0.6 * + cloud-square * to z
	250 seed 3.7 + hash-fraction 450 * + to size
	8 seed 4.9 + hash-fraction 6 * truncate + to n-spheres
	[ 0 n-spheres 1 do k
		seed k 1.3 * + 5.1 + to puff
		size 0.35 puff hash-fraction 0.3 * + * to radius
		puff 0.7 + hash-fraction 0.5 - 2.2 * size * to across
		puff 1.9 + hash-fraction 0.5 - 1.4 * size * to along
		puff 2.6 + hash-fraction 0.6 * size * to rise
		[ x across + cloud-base radius 0.5 * + rise + z along + radius rise size 0.6 * / ]
	loop ] ;

\ one square's cloud's shadow on the ground, [ x z radius ]: its footprint, a circle 1.1 times its size, moved from under it away from the sun, due north, by the base's height over the tangent of the sun's elevation; null when the square is clear
: square-shadow ( column row -- shadow )
	| column row |
	column 7.31 * row 13.17 * + 101 + to seed
	seed hash-fraction cloud-cover >= if null exit then
	column 0.2 + seed 1.1 + hash-fraction 0.6 * + cloud-square * to x
	row 0.2 + seed 2.3 + hash-fraction 0.6 * + cloud-square * to z
	250 seed 3.7 + hash-fraction 450 * + to size
	cloud-base sun-elevation tan / to shift
	[ x z shift + size 1.1 * ] ;

variable cloud-shadows
[ ] to cloud-shadows

\ the clouds near a point: their spheres' centres, radii and shades as columns, and their shadows, gathered when the point crosses into another square
: refresh-clouds ( position -- )
	| position ^cloud-squares ^cloud-square-at ^cloud-centres ^cloud-radii ^cloud-shades ^cloud-shadows |
	position first cloud-square / round-down to column
	position 2 @i cloud-square / round-down to row
	cloud-square-at [ column row ] = if exit then
	[ column row ] to cloud-square-at
	[ ] to near-spheres
	[ ] to cloud-shadows
	column cloud-reach - column cloud-reach + 1 + 1 do c
		row cloud-reach - row cloud-reach + 1 + 1 do r
			c r "{1}/{0}" format string>symbol to key
			cloud-squares key has? not if
				cloud-squares c r square-cloud key ! drop
			then
			near-spheres cloud-squares key @ concat to near-spheres
			c r square-shadow to shadow
			shadow null? not if cloud-shadows shadow add-last! drop then
		loop
	loop
	near-spheres size to n-spheres
	n-spheres 0 = if
		0 4 0-matrix to cloud-centres
		0 1 0-matrix to cloud-radii
		0 1 0-matrix to cloud-shades
		exit
	then
	near-spheres ( sphere | [ sphere first sphere second sphere 2 @i 1 ] ) map flatten n-spheres 4 matrix to cloud-centres
	near-spheres ( sphere | sphere 3 @i ) map vector to cloud-radii
	near-spheres ( sphere | sphere 4 @i ) map vector to cloud-shades ;

\ a disc of cloud in the view: a small one by the window's own disc, a large one in rows cut to the view
: cloud-disc ( x y radius colour -- )
	| x y radius colour |
	radius 40 < if x y radius colour fill-disc exit then
	y radius - 0 max2 round to top
	y radius + view-height min2 round to bottom
	top bottom 2 do row
		radius sq row 1 + y - sq - to room
		room 0 > if
			room sqrt to half
			x half - 0 max2 round to left
			x half + view-width min2 round to right
			right left > if left row right left - 2 colour fill-span then
		then
	loop ;

\ a polygon in the view filled in rows two pixels high, cut to the view: its points [ x y ], in order round it, convex
: fill-polygon ( corners colour -- )
	| corners colour |
	corners ( corner | corner second ) map to ys
	ys 0 ' min2 reduce 0 max2 round to top
	ys -1e9 ' max2 reduce view-height min2 round to bottom
	corners size to n-corners
	top bottom 2 do row
		row 1 + to y
		[ ] to crossings
		0 n-corners 1 do k
			corners k @i to a
			corners k 1+ n-corners mod @i to b
			a second y > b second y > = not if
				crossings y a second - b first a first - * b second a second - / a first + add-last! drop
			then
		loop
		crossings size 2 >= if
			crossings 1e9 ' min2 reduce 0 max2 round to left
			crossings -1e9 ' max2 reduce view-width min2 round to right
			right left > if left row right left - 2 colour fill-span then
		then
	loop ;

\ the clouds' shadows within 10 km and wholly in front of the eye, each its circle on the ground at sea level projected as a sixteen-sided polygon, the ground's or the water's colour three quarters as light, faded with distance as the ground is
: draw-cloud-shadows ( -- )
	eye@position to eye-point
	eye@attitude to attitude
	cloud-shadows ( shadow |
		shadow spread to radius to z to x
		x eye-point first - sq z eye-point 2 @i - sq + sqrt to distance
		distance 10000 < if
			[ 0 16 1 do k
				k 16 / TAU * to angle
				[ x angle sin radius * + 0 z angle cos radius * + ] eye-point v- to offset
				offset attitude@forward v-dot to ahead
				[ view-centre-x focal-length offset attitude@right v-dot * ahead / +
				  view-centre-y focal-length offset attitude@up v-dot * ahead / -
				  ahead ]
			loop ] to corners
			corners ( corner | corner 2 @i near-plane > ) all? if
				x z water-at? if water-colour else level-ground-colour then 0.75 dimmed to shade
				shade sky-colour distance depth-light blended to shade
				corners shade fill-polygon
			then
		then
	) each ;

( draw-cloud-shadows ) to ground-marks

\ the whole scene in one pass from the farthest to the nearest, so that what is filled covers what lies behind it: behind everything the sky, the sun or stars, the ground and the clouds' shadows; then the visible objects of the collections, the hills' slices, the near fields each just after the tile under it, the clouds' spheres in view as discs, and the aircraft given with their smoke, each by its distance along the line of sight; the whole view the cloud's colour when the eye is inside a sphere
: draw-scene ( collections crafts -- )
	| collections crafts ^in-cloud |
	eye@position use-level-ground
	draw-background
	false to in-cloud
	cloud-radii num-elements to n-spheres
	collections object-items terrain-items concat countryside-fields ground-items concat
	town-grounds null? if [ ] else town-grounds ground-items then concat to items
	n-spheres 0 > if
		cloud-centres camera matmul to viewed
		viewed 0 @j to across
		viewed 1 @j to rising
		viewed 2 @j to ahead
		across sq rising sq + ahead sq + to distance-squared
		distance-squared cloud-radii sq < sum 0 > to in-cloud
		ahead near-plane > to in-front
		ahead in-front * 1 in-front - + to safe-ahead
		focal-length across * safe-ahead / view-centre-x + to xs
		view-centre-y focal-length rising * safe-ahead / - to ys
		focal-length cloud-radii * safe-ahead / to rs
		in-front
		xs rs + 0 > *
		xs rs - view-width < *
		ys rs + 0 > *
		ys rs - view-height < *
		distance-squared sqrt cloud-radii - visibility < *
		where to shown
		0 shown num-elements 1 do k
			shown k @e to i
			items [ ahead i @e :cloud i ] add-last! drop
		loop
	then
	crafts ( craft |
		items [ craft@position eye@position v- eye@attitude@forward v-dot :craft craft ] add-last! drop
	) each
	items ( item | item first negate ) sort-by to ordered
	0 ordered size 1 do k
		ordered k @i spread to payload to kind drop
		kind :object = if payload draw-object continue then
		kind :terrain = if payload draw-terrain-tile continue then
		kind :fields = if payload draw-fields continue then
		kind :craft = if payload draw-bomber continue then
		cloud-top-colour cloud-base-colour cloud-shades payload @e blended to colour
		colour sky-colour distance-squared payload @e sqrt depth-light blended to colour
		xs payload @e ys payload @e rs payload @e colour cloud-disc
	loop
	in-cloud if 0 0 view-width view-height cloud-top-colour cloud-base-colour 0.6 blended fill-span then ;
